  "prefLabel": "Env-A 102.46 Combustion device",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 102.46 “Combustion device” means any device, including incinerators, boilers, turbines and engines, as well as asphalt plant dryers and miscellaneous combustion sources, that discharge air pollutants into the ambient air as a result of a combustion process.\n\nSource. #6983-A, eff 4-23-99; renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.75), see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading; renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.46), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.47) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
